  message: "Merged in PR #1517 (286c579b0a): README.md (and the identical packages/hypergumbo/README.md) gains '## Security and trust (as of 2026-10)' plus a pointer under pip install. Covers: agent-written / not line-reviewed (5,410 of 5,483 non-tracker commits by the agent account; ~287k src / ~600k test lines by wc -l over tracked .py, 2026-10-10 — differs from the 349k/508k figure in this item, which used an unstated method); default-run reads/writes/subprocesses (verified by strace on a tiny repo: only git, gitleaks, rust-analyzer --version; 0 connect() with models cached); the first-sketch HF model download after install-embeddings (INV-gujus); install-*/add-extras/build-grammars; rust-analyzer backend enabled by flag, env or trust-backend grant, never config (ADR-0045); scip-python enableable by the analysed repo's .hypergumbo.toml (INV-tusos); htrac not in the meta-package, sync/auto-sync, serve without auth (WI-hopip), OpenRouter (WI-puban), not self-audited (WI-sunan, ADR-0013); both CI gates and their open findings; untrusted-repo influence (ADR-0061, new INV-nihab); confinement (strace recipe verified; docker and macOS recipes described without full commands because neither could be run here). Side findings filed: INV-bazoz (build-grammars cannot work from a PyPI install), INV-nihab (gitleaks unlinks /dev/stdout as root; reads repo .gitleaks.toml). Keep the section current as INV-gujus/tusos/kuroj and WI-sunan/hopip land."  # 71d9
